# Go
*.exe
*.test
*.out
renderinggen/renderinggen
renderinggen/render-showcase
renderinggen/bin/
/bin/
.tmp/
renderinggen/.tmp/
queue/queued
queue/bin/
objectstore/objectstore
objectstore/bin/

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Env / secrets
.env
*.local.yaml

# Google service-account keys (never commit)
*gcp-service-account*.json
*service-account*.json
*.credentials.json

# Google Drive OAuth client + token (never commit)
credentials.json
token.json

# Generated render/benchmark artifacts
# Per-frame telemetry sidecars are pure diagnostics: a render regenerates them
# on demand, each one is ~1.2 MB of per-frame JSON, and they are the bulk of
# the artifact bloat here. They are never committed in any directory, not just
# the roots enumerated below.
*.mp4.timing.json
*.mp4.telemetry-summary.json
/renderinggen/*.mp4
/renderinggen/*.mp4.timing.json
/renderinggen/*.mp4.receipt.json
/renderinggen/*_plan.json
/renderinggen/concurrent_test_videos/
/renderinggen/modern_preset_videos/
/renderinggen/phrase_preset_videos/
/renderinggen/preset_videos/
/renderinggen/highend_phrase_videos/
/renderinggen/warm_videos/
# Top-level preset/demo renders (were tracked as 37 MB bloat, D5): keep on
# disk but never in git — same artifact class as /renderinggen/* variants.
# .gitignore only covered /renderinggen/*.mp4 + 5 subdirs, not these roots.
/preset_videos/
/phrase_preset_videos/
# typewriter_phrase_videos was the last tracked top-level demo root (52 files,
# ~7 MB of mp4/timing/plan). Same class as the two above: on disk, never in git.
/typewriter_phrase_videos/
# apple_style_final_videos is the same artifact class again: rendered clips plus
# their sidecars, reproducible from the crime/discovery/young style presets.
/apple_style_final_videos/
# phrase_overlay_v3 is the modern v3 phrase matrix: reproducible from
# cmd/batch-render-presets/phrase-overlay-v3-manifest.json, so the rendered mp4s
# and their plan pairs stay on disk and out of git.
/phrase_overlay_v3/
# phrase_animations_v1 is the real-phrase animation matrix: the ten editorial
# phrase candidates, one apple_v2 motion each, reproducible from
# cmd/batch-render-presets/phrase-animations-v1-manifest.json — same artifact
# class as phrase_overlay_v3 above.
/phrase_animations_v1/
# mike_tyson_overlay_test is a manual smoke scenario: its request/plan/script
# JSON and input media are worth keeping, but output/ holds the rendered mp4s
# that a re-run regenerates on demand — the same artifact class as above.
/mike_tyson_overlay_test/output/

# Localized 10×10 certification reruns keep large media and queue snapshots
# available for inspection without checking generated artifacts into git. The
# manifest and compact JSON reports remain reviewable versioned evidence.
/multilingual_overlays_v1/artifacts_*/
/multilingual_overlays_v1/plans_*/
/multilingual_overlays_v1/verify/
/multilingual_overlays_v1/jobs_snapshot_*.json
assets/backgrounds/*.mp4
!assets/backgrounds/background-boxe.mp4
!assets/backgrounds/background-crime.mp4
!assets/backgrounds/background-music.mp4
!assets/backgrounds/background-wwe.mp4
!assets/backgrounds/background-discovery.mp4

# Keep testdata/golden intentionally tiny: only canonical CI/regression fixtures.
/testdata/golden/*
!/testdata/golden/DejaVuSans.ttf
!/testdata/golden/Poppins-Bold.ttf
!/testdata/golden/apple.png
!/testdata/golden/background.jpg
!/testdata/golden/background.mp4
!/testdata/golden/golden-overlay-job-v1.json
!/testdata/golden/golden-overlay-job-v2.json
!/testdata/golden/golden-semantic-overlay-job-v1.json
!/testdata/golden/logo_pulse.png
!/testdata/golden/overlay_chart.png
!/testdata/golden/overlay_globe.png

# Debug scratch (plan dumps used while diagnosing the render graph) and
# Python bytecode are never committed.
/testdata/debug/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Top-level out/ holds certification rerun renders (mp4 + logs + timing
# sidecars): generated evidence a re-run regenerates on demand — same
# artifact class as the /preset_videos/ family above. On disk, never in git.
/out/
# Same artifact class, but under the Go module root (274 MB of editorial_v1 /
# map_motion renders, timing sidecars and copied fonts).
/renderinggen/out/

# production_rehearsal_v1 is the localized 10×10 certification rerun tree. Its
# rendered clips are the same artifact class as the /out and artifacts_* /
# plans_* families above — a re-run regenerates them from the manifests — but
# they were never covered, so each run re-added 76 mp4 under nested
# *_artifacts*//*_timing* dirs. The patterns below ignore ONLY the media: the
# per-run manifests and compact reports at the tree root stay reviewable
# versioned evidence, which is the same split the artifacts_*/plans_* rules
# above already make.
/multilingual_overlays_v1/production_rehearsal_v1/**/*.mp4

# mike_tyson_overlay_test keeps its request/plan/script JSON and the input
# assets (all reviewable); only the preset gallery's rendered clips are the
# artifact class. /mike_tyson_overlay_test/output/ is already ignored above,
# but preset_overlays_v1/renders/ was not, so a gallery re-run re-added mp4.
/mike_tyson_overlay_test/preset_overlays_v1/renders/
